---
description: Shader and VFX technique defaults for mobile casual games
globs: ["**/*.shadergraph", "**/*.shader", "**/*.cs"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Don't default to VFX Graph for mobile-targeted effects — it needs compute shaders,
  which are unreliable on low/mid-end Android GPUs. Do: use Shuriken particle systems for
  mobile, unless I've said the target is PC/console.
- Don't hand-write HLSL unless Shader Graph genuinely can't do it. Do: default to Shader
  Graph and explain if HLSL is truly needed.
- Do: name a real comparison point when proposing an effect (e.g. "this is the
  anticipation glow before a slot jackpot symbol lands") so it's grounded in an actual
  casual-mobile-game convention, not invented generically.
